# Fontly content rules

## Two collections, from the start

- src/content/pages/ for the seventeen tool pages and the homepage
- src/content/blog/ for blog posts

Both are declared in `src/content.config.ts`, not in `src/content/config.ts`.
Astro 7 moved the file. Every collection also needs an explicit loader, so each
one is defined with `loader: glob(...)` pointing at its own folder. Create both
in the first phase, even though the blog is built later. Retrofitting a second
collection later means touching routing.

## Frontmatter schema for pages

Define it with Zod so a bad page fails the build instead of shipping broken.

- title, string, the title tag, maximum 60 characters, validated
- h1, string, the visible heading, may differ from the title
- description, string, meta description, maximum 155 characters, validated
- no `slug` field at all. Astro reserves `slug`, and putting it in a Zod schema
  throws `ContentSchemaContainsSlugError`. The URL comes from the filename
  instead, so the file is named for the slug and `index.md` is the homepage
- primaryKeyword, string
- toolCategories, ordered array of category ids. Each id must exist in
  src/data/categories.ts. This is the list of tool sections that page
  renders, in order — not a yes/no switch that turns the tool on.
- testPhrase, optional string, the input prefill for that page's tool
- heroIntro, optional string, short copy under the h1 and above the tool.
  Comes from the owner's Notion article and is never written by an agent.
  Omit the field (and the element) when absent.
- faq, array of objects with q and a, defaults to an empty array, never required
- relatedTools, array of page slugs, not URLs, defaults to an empty array,
  never required
- publishedDate, optional date
- updatedDate, optional date

The blog collection uses the same shape minus toolCategories, plus a
required date.

## Who may create page files

Never create a new Markdown file for a real page on your own initiative,
and never invent a title, description, H1 or FAQ. Articles are written by
the owner outside this repository. You may create a page file only when the
owner supplies the exact frontmatter values in the prompt, and in that case
the body must stay a single clearly marked placeholder line until the owner
pastes the real article.

## Rules that must hold structurally

- The faq array feeds two things from one source: the visible accordion and
  the FAQPage JSON-LD. A FAQ is never written twice.
- relatedTools holds slugs. RelatedTools reads the content collection and
  takes each link's text from that page's own frontmatter title. A slug with
  no entry in the collection is omitted, never rendered as a dead link. A
  hand-written copy of page titles is banned. An earlier prototype shipped
  eleven related-tool links where nine were 404s; that must now be
  structurally impossible.
- Use plain independent <details> elements for the FAQ, not a
  one-at-a-time accordion. Answers stay in the HTML source when collapsed.
- In-body internal links are absolute URLs, so they return 404 until every
  page exists. Add a build-time link checker that fails the build.

## Converting an article from Notion into Markdown

Articles are written in Notion by the owner and converted, never written
here. An agent asked to write article copy will invent the very facts these
articles were written to debunk. Do not write, extend, summarise or improve
article prose. Convert only.

Delete these before converting:

- the yellow progress callout
- the red pre-publish checklist
- the blue self-audit callout
- everything from the Phase 9 header downwards

Do not delete the tool embed token (for example BUBBLE_TOOL_EMBED). Replace the
whole token line with the single line TOOL PLACEHOLDER, which is the marker the
route splits on to mount the tool.

Lift these into frontmatter: title tag, meta description, H1, primary keyword.

Move the FAQ out of the body and into the faq array as q and a pairs.

Turn "More Font Tools" into relatedTools slugs.

Do not paste JSON-LD into the Markdown. Schema.astro generates it.

## Titles and meta descriptions are already written

Every title tag and meta description was written and character-counted by
hand in Notion. Copy them verbatim. Do not rewrite, shorten, optimise or
regenerate them. If one exceeds the Zod limit, report it and stop rather
than editing it yourself.

## Keyword ownership

- One page, one primary keyword, one H1. Never reuse a primary keyword.
- The homepage primary keyword is "cool fonts". It is not
  "font generator copy paste", which an older draft used.
- Long-tail questions become FAQ entries or H2 sections on an existing
  page, never new pages.
- Cannibalisation is defined by search intent, not by shared words.
